From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:09:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipmr: do not drop GSO packets that fit the MTU after segmentation

ipmr_prepare_xmit() drops DF packets larger than route MTU without
checking skb_is_gso() and skb_gso_validate_network_len(), dropping
fraglist/UDP GRO multicast aggregates as FragFails. Validate segmented
GSO packet length against mtu - encap just like ip_forward().

Fixes: 9fd1ff5d2ac7 ("udp: Support UDP fraglist GRO/GSO.")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/cover.1792293419.git.julius@bairaktaris.de/
Origin: archive/xr1710g-v1@e85677d284c0
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/net/ipv4/ipmr.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/ipmr.c
@@ -1937,6 +1937,7 @@ static int ipmr_prepare_xmit(struct net
 	struct rtable *rt;
 	struct flowi4 fl4;
 	int    encap = 0;
+	unsigned int mtu;
 
 	vif_dev = vif_dev_read(vif);
 	if (!vif_dev)
@@ -1969,7 +1970,10 @@ static int ipmr_prepare_xmit(struct net
 			return -1;
 	}
 
-	if (skb->len+encap > dst4_mtu(&rt->dst) && (ntohs(iph->frag_off) & IP_DF)) {
+	mtu = dst4_mtu(&rt->dst);
+	if (skb->len + encap > mtu && (ntohs(iph->frag_off) & IP_DF) &&
+	    !(skb_is_gso(skb) && mtu > encap &&
+	      skb_gso_validate_network_len(skb, mtu - encap))) {
 		/* Do not fragment multicasts. Alas, IPv4 does not
 		 * allow to send ICMP, so that packets will disappear
 		 * to blackhole.
